&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harbor&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;/span&gt;looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Intapp Implementation Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to lead the design, configuration and delivery of Intapp solutions for legal-sector clients. You will work with client stakeholders across IT, Risk and Compliance, Finance and legal teams to turn business needs into secure, practical solutions across the matter lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone with substantial experience implementing and enhancing Intapp products in a law-firm environment. You will take ownership of complex workstreams, guide technical decisions and support other members of the delivery team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end Intapp implementation work, from discovery and requirements through solution design, configuration, testing, deployment and post-go-live support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and enhance workflows, forms, rules and application configurations for client and matter intake, conflicts, risk and compliance, time recording or related processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on solution options, product capabilities, design trade-offs and implementation approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and support relevant Intapp products, such as Intapp Intake, Conflicts, Open, Time, Walls, Flow and Integrate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and oversee integrations with legal finance, document management and other business systems, including integration testing and defect resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead workshops with business and technical stakeholders; document requirements, process flows, functional designs and technical specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and coordinate system testing, user acceptance testing, data validation, training, deployment and business readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex issues and work with client teams and Intapp support to resolve product or implementation problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve workflows, controls, data quality and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance to junior engineers and contribute to delivery standards, documentation and estimates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support upgrades, migration planning and cloud readiness where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years of hands-on experience implementing, configuring or significantly enhancing Intapp products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering Intapp solutions in a law firm or comparable professional-services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven participation in multiple implementation or major enhancement projects, with responsibility for solution design and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of one or more Intapp products, such as Intake, Conflicts, Open, Time, Walls, Flow or Integrate. Depth in a core product is essential; experience across several products is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing workflows and translating Risk, Compliance, Finance or legal business requirements into technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with integrations between Intapp and other enterprise or legal-sector systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence leading workshops, managing stakeholders and explaining technical choices clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning or carrying out testing, deployments, upgrades and post-go-live support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, documentation and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
